      en: "The Chu River is a major 1,067-kilometer-long river traversing northern Kyrgyzstan. It originates in the Kochkor Valley and flows through the spectacular Boom Gorge before entering the expansive, agriculturally rich Chu Valley. A significant portion of the river forms the natural border between Kyrgyzstan and Kazakhstan. The river is endorheic; it does not flow into any ocean but eventually disappears into the sands of the Muyunkum Desert in southern Kazakhstan. Its waters are essential for irrigation in both countries."
