      en: "Besh-Tash National Park is located in the northwestern Talas Province of Kyrgyzstan. Established in 1996, the park protects a diverse mountain landscape ranging from deep valleys at 1,100 meters to high alpine peaks at 3,600 meters. The name 'Besh-Tash' translates to 'Five Stones', referring to five prominent rock formations found in the area. At the heart of the park lies the beautiful alpine Besh-Tash Lake. The protected area provides a critical habitat for a rich variety of flora and fauna, including the rare snow leopard, brown bears, and numerous endemic plant species."
